{"status":"unsupported_domain","reason":"A faithful contract cannot be expressed in the admitted typed AST and executable Python test bridge without changing the specified JSON representation.","gaps":[{"obligations":["D1","A1"],"description":"Each edge is a positional JSON array [u,v,cost] with nonnegative vertex indices and a signed integer cost. The frontend has homogeneous lists and named records, but no fixed positional tuple sort or registered array-to-tuple serialization."},{"obligations":["O1","O2","O3","O4","O5","S1"],"description":"The output is a single length-n JSON array whose entries are integer distances, JSON null, or the exact string \"-inf\". The frontend has no union sort with this JSON serialization. Unit, records, or Except cannot silently replace these observable values."},{"obligations":["S2","R1"],"description":"The formula grammar cannot express Python execution effects, retained state, file and network access, printing, or library dependencies. These requirements need registered implementation checks."}],"required_extension":"Register faithful positional edge serialization, a distance union serialized directly as integer/null/\"-inf\", and executable checks for purity and standard-library-only dependencies. Then retain all graph, shortest-walk, negative-cycle propagation, ordering, example, and assumption-witness obligations.","preserved_obligations":["D1","A1","O1","O2","O3","O4","O5","S1","S2","R1"]}